> Can I polypile them to get a luck stone? Is it a waste to use up
> my wand?  What kind of stones do I need to zap?

In theory, yes, you can. In practice, no, it's a waste of your wand.

The chance of polying a magical stone into a non-magical one is 92%; the
chance of polying a non-magical stone into a magical one is, as the
Hugo-O'Donnell spoiler puts it, negligible. Since luckstones are magical
and gems are not, you could start with a pile of touchstones, zap your
/oPoly empty, and you'd probably end up with a lot of opals and glass
and not a single luckstone.

